# Agent token hygiene

## Blocked paths (do not read, grep, diff, or secret-scan)

- `view/static/assets/**` — minified JS/CSS bundles
- `model/assets/**` — media manifests and binaries
- `model/validation/**` — local recordings and learner data
- `config/client_secret_*.json`, `analysis.txt`

Exception: only when the user explicitly asks about deploy bundles, hash mismatches, or asset deployment.

## Frontend build workflow

After a Vite/static build:

- Check `view/static/index.html` for new hashed asset names
- Stage/commit source + `index.html` + new bundle files
- Do **not** open `.js` or `.css` under `view/static/assets/`

## Search and commit hygiene

- Prefer targeted `rg` on source paths (`view/app/`, `backend/`, `tests/`)
- Never run secret scans or broad searches across `view/static/assets/`
- Use `git diff --stat` before focused `git diff` on 1–3 source files
- Prefer `python scripts/summarize_content_json.py` over opening broad `model/content/**/*.json`
- Prefer focused pytest (`-k`, single file) over full suite unless required

## Skills

- Do not re-read attached skill files if instructions are already in context
- Post-commit review gate: if `POST-COMMIT REVIEW GATE` is injected, use that block only — do not open the skill file
